# paramvaswani-site

Personal site for Param Vaswani. One self-contained file, vanilla JS, no framework,
no build step, no dependencies. Read `EDITING.md` for the file map and `HANDOFF.md`
for settled decisions and the ship-gates before changing anything substantive.

## Format — break this and publishing breaks

`index.html`, `figure-legend.html`, and `POSITION.html` are **artifact fragments**:
`<title>` on line 1, then `<link>`, `<style>`, markup, `<script>`.

**There is deliberately no `<!doctype>`, `<html>`, `<head>`, or `<body>` tag.** The
publish wrapper adds them; `dev.py` adds the same wrapper locally. Never "fix" this by
adding them. Verify with `grep -c '<body' index.html` → must be 0.

## Running it

```bash
./dev.py          # → localhost:4173, live: edit + refresh, no build
```

Routes: `/` site · `/legend` · `/position` · `/_pages` index.
There is no npm, no package.json, no bundler. Don't add one.

Use a real browser. Some embedded preview panes suspend `requestAnimationFrame`, which
makes the Galton machine, drift balls, and breakout look frozen — that's the pane, not a bug.

## Engine rules

- **All animation goes through the hybrid clocks** — `fixedLoop` / `frameLoop`, between the
  `clocks:begin` / `clocks:end` markers. They render on rAF in real browsers but keep a
  `setInterval` watchdog so rAF-less documents still tick. Physics steps at a fixed 30 ms so
  the Node-verified simulations stay valid. Don't call `requestAnimationFrame` or
  `setInterval` directly for new animation — use the clocks.
- **Keep every `prefers-reduced-motion` fallback.** Each animated figure has a static state
  that still communicates its claim. New motion needs one too.
- No per-frame `getComputedStyle` and no per-event `querySelectorAll` — both were removed
  for latency. Cache lookups outside the loop.

## Venn geometry (fig. 1) — two sources of truth

Circle positions exist **twice**: as SVG attributes (`cx/cy/r` on `.tint`, `.halo`, `.set`,
and the `clipPath` defs) and in the JS `sets` array used for hit-testing. Change one, change
both, or hover detection silently desyncs from what's drawn.

**Only label an intersection that geometrically exists.** Five circles cannot represent all
31 combinations. Seven regions exist and are labeled. Before adding or moving a label, run
the region scan in `EDITING.md` and confirm real area.

## Content rules (from the audit — don't regress these)

- **fig. 3 edges:** only `feed ↔ me` and (weakly) `machines ↔ me` are bidirectional. Every
  other edge is one-way and labeled as such. Do not re-inflate to "every edge runs both ways."
- **Privacy is a hard limit.** No health, diagnoses, medication, family, or third parties.
  The society card's existing abstraction is the ceiling. Contact is `hello@paramvaswani.com`
  only. Three withholding moves, no fourth. No redaction theatrics.
- **RLHF register: exactly two touches** — "Raised by the algorithm, realigning by hand" and
  the word "overcorrection" on fig. 2. The acronym never appears.

## Publishing

The live render is a **private Claude artifact**:
`https://claude.ai/code/artifact/ab79be5a-60b8-4126-809b-90f0556f70e5`

Cursor cannot publish to it — that needs the Artifact tool in Claude Code. Edit here, commit,
and publish from Claude Code (pass the URL as `url` so it updates in place instead of
creating a duplicate).

**Do not deploy to a public URL.** Ship-gates in `HANDOFF.md` are unmet — the domain
`paramvaswani.com` is still unregistered, and fonts need self-hosting before anything public.
Private commits are fine; public surfaces need Param to say so explicitly.

## Sanity checks after editing

```bash
python3 -c "import re;s=open('index.html').read();print('div',len(re.findall(r'<div\b',s)),len(re.findall(r'</div>',s)));print('svg',s.count('<svg'),s.count('</svg>'))"
head -1 index.html && grep -c '<body' index.html   # want <title>… and 0
```

Then load in a real browser and confirm the console is clean.
